{
 "_doc": "'since <event>' anchors (spec v1.8 10g.29, 10g.31). The event phrase runs from 'since' to the next punctuation or connector. A phrase with a date keeps the normal window rules (10g.29: the date binds). Without a date: data_start (regex, from the phrase start; 'my first reading/test', also 'my first blood/lab test', 10g.31) -> all_history trend; a device start (exactly one wearable alias from source_aliases.json, not a lab_sources id, plus a device_start_verbs word) -> all_history + that source, trend, only when the source is valid for every read metric; account_start or restart words, or any other event -> handoff (unresolved_temporal_phrase). back_reference ('since then') is left to the follow-up rules (10g.26 (c)). medical words in the sentence of a 'since' phrase hand off even with a date (10g.28 class 2, 10g.29); matched on word boundaries.",
